<title>UK: SmithKline shares rise on drug approval.</title>
<headline>SmithKline shares rise on drug approval.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in pharmaceutical company SmithKline Beecham advanced on Thursday following news that the U.S. FDA had cleared the manufacture of Infanrix.</p>
<p>The shares rose sharply on the news, to be up 25-1/2p at 873-1/2p by 1443 GMT.  </p>
<p>Earlier, the company said the FDA had granted SmithKline Beecham Biologicals a license to manufacture the vaccine for immunisation against diphtheria, tetanus and whooping cough.</p>
<p>Infanix is now licensed in more than 10 countries.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
